From: BeagleY AI integration <noreply@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] tiovx: skip TI 2A processing when AE and AWB are disabled

The current postprocess path always invokes TI_2A_wrapper_process(), then
checks the AE mode afterwards. This prevents a fixed exposure/gain mode
from bypassing the 2A processing cost and can also fail before reaching
the explicit-mode check when DCC calibration data is invalid.

Skip the complete 2A postprocess when every sink requests disabled AE and
AWB. The VISS pipeline continues to produce NV12 using its configured
static tuning.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [BeagleY camera bring-up]

--- a/ext/tiovx/gsttiovxisp.c
+++ b/ext/tiovx/gsttiovxisp.c
@@ -2251,6 +2251,19 @@
   self = GST_TIOVX_ISP (miso);
   sink_pads_list = GST_ELEMENT (miso)->sinkpads;
 
+  for (l = sink_pads_list; l != NULL; l = g_list_next (l)) {
+    GstTIOVXIspPad *sink_pad = (GstTIOVXIspPad *) l->data;
+    if (sink_pad->ae_mode != ALGORITHMS_ISS_AE_DISABLED ||
+        sink_pad->awb_mode != ALGORITHMS_ISS_AWB_DISABLED) {
+      break;
+    }
+  }
+  if (NULL == l) {
+    GST_LOG_OBJECT (self, "AE and AWB disabled; skipping TI 2A processing");
+    ret = TRUE;
+    goto exit;
+  }
+
   if (postprocess_skip_frames >= ++self->postprocess_iter) {
     GST_LOG_OBJECT (self, "Skipping postprocess iteration #%d",
         self->postprocess_iter);
